OPEN PILANTRA — attribution and provenance
==========================================

This repository contains two distinct bodies of work. Please keep them
straight when reusing anything from it.


1. The original demo — © Erico Patricio Monteiro (FUED.NET), 2026
-----------------------------------------------------------------

    OPIL-source.bas         ugBASIC source for the demo
    OPIL-EN.dsk             English build, RS-DOS disk image
    OPIL_BR.dsk             Brazilian Portuguese build (the original)
    OPEN PILANTRA.pdf       the author's manual
    docs/art/*.png          figures clipped from that manual

Written, drawn, scripted and documented by Erico Patricio Monteiro, who
releases under the name FUED.NET.

    Project page:  https://fued.net/open-pilantra/

The author distributes the demo freely, with source code and the manual,
and the manual states:

    "Open Pilantra is made so people can play around with it, you are
     free to change graphics, dialogs or add anything you please."

These files are mirrored here under that stated intent so the repository
stays self-contained and buildable. No separate licence grant has been
obtained. If you are the author and would prefer they were removed or
handled differently, please open an issue and it will be done promptly.

If you enjoy the work, the author asks that you consider donating to
support future projects. Please do that through fued.net rather than
treating this mirror as the source.

The demo was shown at RetroSC 2025 by the author, and at COCO Fest 2026
by Henry Strickland.


